data.reasoningText:
The serialize side uses `writer.WriteObjectValue(Error, options)`. But `ResponseError` might not implement `IJsonModel<T>` - it would fall through the switch in `WriteObjectValue` and potentially not work. Let me check what `WriteObjectValue` does for types that aren't IJsonModel...

Looking at the WriteObjectValue method from earlier:
```csharp
case IJsonModel<T> jsonModel:
    jsonModel.Write(writer, options ?? WireOptions);
    break;
case IUtf8JsonSerializable serializable:
    serializable.Write(writer);
    break;
```

If ResponseError doesn't implement either of these interfaces, it would fall through and fail. I should change the Error serialization to use the source-gen context directly with `JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, Error, ResourceManagerInternalJsonContext.Default.ResponseError)` instead.

